The test file parametrizes 10 direct calls to `Qtile._process_screens` and always builds `DummyConfig` with a `fake_screens` attribute only when `use_fake` is true, but every listed case has `use_fake: False`, so execution always skips the `fake_screens` block and enters the core-screen-info deduplication path. The cases collectively cover both reusing configured screens and creating a new `Screen()`, setting `current_screen` when absent or when `reloading` is true, taking the existing-group path and the available-group path, taking both outcomes of `if grp is None`, taking both outcomes of `if not hasattr(scr, "group")`, computing `reconfigure_gaps` as both true and false, calling `_configure`, appending each screen, iterating stale old screens, and finalizing only bar gaps with windows. That leaves uncovered only the `fake_screens` lines and the autogen-group assignment line.

